
 • This method works when the array elements are in the range 1 to n (length of the array).
 • It’s in-place, O(n) time, O(1) extra space, and finds all duplicates.

1. Idea of Cyclic Sort for Duplicates
=======================================

    • For an array of length n, each number num should ideally be at index: num - 1.
    • Swap each number to its correct index until all numbers are either:
          • in their correct place, or
          • duplicates (because the correct place already has that number).
    • After this, any number i not at index i-1 is a duplicate.